# Provenance of the bundled basic-webserver corpus.
#
# Update this file each time you refresh this directory, so that the next
# refresh can diff tag-to-tag and apply the patch series again.

repo     https://github.com/roc-lang/basic-webserver
tag      0.19.0
commit   1654ae3
tarball  4KBAoiBazDfi9UF6e3BYKwon6rA8mnx3dbLMLKFzdEMw.tar.zst

# This platform re-exports the same roc-lang/http release that basic-cli pins. Its index is at corpus/packages/http/, with its provenance
# in corpus/packages/http/UPSTREAM.

# The nightly of this release: upstream's .roc-version at the tag. Every app
# below pins its platform by tarball URL, and the gates check each program that
# pins this release with this nightly. A program with a `roc:` line of its own
# uses that nightly. So this line moves only when the platform is repinned, and
# not when the bundled nightly moves.
compiler nightly-2026-10-24-f6c6cfb

index.json <- platform/   parsed by `npm run build:index` from the compiler's
                         package cache. Signatures and docstrings only; no
                         source is vendored
examples/  <- examples/*.roc + todos.html
docs/      <- docs/sse.md, docs/benchmarking.md

# These files are ours and come from the files above, so read them again on a
# refresh. Each one pins the URLs in the block above:
#   topics/       complete apps served as syntax topics
#   scaffold.roc  the app roc_check wraps bare code in
#   verify/       every overview snippet, in one app
#   overview.md   the page get_roc_syntax(scope:) returns
#
# The repinning checklist is in
# .claude/skills/refresh-roc-upstream/reference/basic-webserver.md.

# The examples tree is the patched result, not an exact copy of upstream. The
# patches make it again from a fresh checkout of the tag:
#
#   patch -p1 < patches/0001-repin-examples-*.patch
#   patch -p1 < patches/0002-restore-parked-gregorian-examples.patch
#
# 0001 is necessary, because every example at tag 0.19.0 pins platform 0.17.0
# (the five parked ones, 0.16.0).
# 0002 restores the five examples that upstream still disables as `.todoroc`
# (command, echo, error-handling, file-accessed-modified-created-time,
# init-basic). Upstream restored hello-web in 0.19.0, so the patch no longer
# touches it. The five depend on gregorian 1.0.0-rc.3, which the compiler
# rejects for its redundant return-position `..` unions. The patch renames each file back to `.roc` and removes upstream's
# TODO preamble, the gregorian dependency and its import. Where gregorian
# formatted an ISO 8601 string, the patch prints
# `seconds_since_epoch().to_str()`. It also moves their `roc:` line from
# c507926 to f6c6cfb, because platform 0.19.0 does not build on c507926
# (`Json.invalid_json` takes an argument there). Delete the patch when
# gregorian has a release that builds. Under nightly f6c6cfb, gregorian gives ten warnings,
# five for redundant open unions and five for redundant returns.
#
# The examples keep upstream's `roc:` line, f6c6cfb. Each example passes
# `roc check` on the nightly it pins, with the two patches applied. On another nightly, the compiler warns and names the
# pinned one, so an agent that copies an example learns which nightly to run.

# Not bundled, by choice:
#   design.md     contributor-facing architecture prose
#   README.md     overview.md replaces it
#   examples/datastar/   a separate multi-module app, not a single file
#   examples/todos.db*   binary fixtures
